(a) exports as Elixir sees them:
  Shop exports                                [Amount: 1, Band: 1, Bump: 1, New: 1, Pay: 1, Squared: 1, Total: 1, Which: 1, bs@type_atoms: 0]
(b) a B# record arrives as:
  value                                       %{Kind: :"Shop.Order", Id: 7, Total: 0}
  is_struct?                                  false
  map pattern %{Kind: :"Shop.Order", Id: id}  {:matched, 7}
(c) handing values back (right tag / wrong tag / struct), via the quoted call:
  right tag                                   :order
  wrong tag                                   {:raised, FunctionClauseError}
  Elixir struct, same fields                  {:raised, FunctionClauseError}
  NEGATIVE CONTROL: right tag, missing Total  :order
